  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A thermodynamic system is taken from an original state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> to an intermediate state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> by a linear process as shown in the figure. Its volume is then reduced to the original value from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> by an isobaric process. The total work done by the gas from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> would be :</p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2a96272b-4254-4cee-84b3-193b8206f736.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 222px;\"/>",
    "image": null
  },
